<Doc lang={lang} page="blocks" current="Astrometry" title="Astrometry"
  description="The Astrometry block of FLOAT: plate solving of the stack, a first solution then a fine fit on Gaia DR3 stars, what the solution serves, the offline star catalogue, settings and limits, with the published sources.">

  <p class="kicker">Block</p>
  <h1>Astrometry</h1>
  <p class="meta">FLOAT 0.2.0 · beta of {release.date.en}</p>

  <dl class="inshort"><div><dt>What it does</dt><dd>It recognises the patch of sky in the stack from its stars, so that every pixel gets its position on the sky, and the later blocks can use the star catalogue.</dd></div><div><dt>What it shows</dt><dd>In Inspect, the image with the sky grid and the catalogue stars set on its stars, with the image scale, the field of view, the position residual and the focal length found; in the Report, the target, the field and the scale.</dd></div><div><dt>What can be set</dt><dd>Usually nothing, when the files hold the pointing and the focal length; otherwise give the Target name, or the Focal length.</dd></div></dl>

