    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="s7"><span class="secnum">7</span>Limits, and what was tried</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>A wrong focal length does not hide the field.</strong> When the field is not found at the scale of the
      entered focal length, it is searched again without it. A warning says the field is at another scale, and to check
      the focal length and the pixel size.</li>
      <li><strong>Blind solving needs its index.</strong> When the star index is not installed, the all-sky search
      cannot try, and the block asks for the target or its coordinates.</li>
      <li><strong>Narrow fields are hard to solve blind.</strong> The blind solver is built for wide fields, with enough
      bright stars in them.</li>
      <li><strong>Unknown scale and far centre can take minutes.</strong> Without Asterion, an unknown scale means a
      search over 22 scales. A match at another scale than the trial one is followed
      at once, to avoid walking the whole grid.</li>
      <li><strong>Sparse fields.</strong> Under 50 stars, a solution needs strong proof and has no distortion polynomial.
      A field that does not give it has no solution.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

